.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-collection 1  "tapectl-collection " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-collection \- Manage media collections (folder=unit factory + batch tape driver)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl collection\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage media collections (folder=unit factory + batch tape driver)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-collection\-sync(1)
Sync every configured collection: register new unit folders, resolve moved/renamed ones by dotfile uuid, mark vanished ones `missing` (never deleted or retired — those are operator acts)
.TP
tapectl\-collection\-status(1)
Show pending/dirty/missing/under\-copied counts for every configured collection
.TP
tapectl\-collection\-plan(1)
Show the batch plan (alphabetical first\-fit, §7) for every configured collection\*(Aqs pending units
.TP
tapectl\-collection\-run(1)
Execute one batch: stage every unit in it once, write one session per destination label, then release staging. Targets a single collection (unlike `sync`/`status`/`plan`, which sweep every configured collection) since a batch write is a real, one\-shot tape action
.TP
tapectl\-collection\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
